Usage:
  nucleus new <project_name> [flags]

Create a new project scaffold: go.mod pinned to this release, a composition-root main.go, nucleus.yml and an empty migrations directory. The mvc and api templates generate no feature code; the suite template carries a worked shop module on the Quark ORM with the Orbit admin panel mounted. The module template writes a module repository instead of an application.

Arguments:
  <project_name>  Directory created under --out; also the default module path suffix (example.com/<project_name>)

Templates (--template):
  mvc     Full-stack: default subsystems, rbac_policy.csv and the driver import for --db (default)
  api     Core-only: WithoutDefaults(), no admin, mail or authz; storage only once nucleus.yml declares it (WithStorage)
  suite   Nucleus + Quark + Orbit wired together: a shop module on the Quark ORM, the admin panel under /admin, Data Studio and the live SQL feed (implies --with of all four suite modules)
  module  A module repository of its own, for an application to Mount: go.mod, the module (a route, its policy row, typed configuration, a value it provides), a test that calls nucleustest.CheckModule, a README and a CI workflow that runs go test (--db, --port and --with do not apply)

Catalog entries (--with, comma-separated; the names nucleus add takes):
  postgres         database driver (github.com/jcsvwinston/nucleus/drivers/postgres): fetched at the version released with this CLI and imported in main.go
  mysql            database driver (github.com/jcsvwinston/nucleus/drivers/mysql): fetched at the version released with this CLI and imported in main.go
  sqlite           database driver (github.com/jcsvwinston/nucleus/drivers/sqlite): fetched at the version released with this CLI and imported in main.go
  sqlserver        database driver (github.com/jcsvwinston/nucleus/drivers/mssql): fetched at the version released with this CLI and imported in main.go
  oracle           database driver (github.com/jcsvwinston/nucleus/drivers/oracle): fetched at the version released with this CLI and imported in main.go
  otlp             telemetry exporter (github.com/jcsvwinston/nucleus/exporters/otlp): fetched at the version released with this CLI and imported in main.go
  prometheus       telemetry exporter (github.com/jcsvwinston/nucleus/exporters/prometheus): fetched at the version released with this CLI and imported in main.go
  s3               storage provider (github.com/jcsvwinston/nucleus/providers/storage-s3): fetched at the version released with this CLI and imported in main.go
  gcs              storage provider (github.com/jcsvwinston/nucleus/providers/storage-gcs): fetched at the version released with this CLI and imported in main.go
  azure            storage provider (github.com/jcsvwinston/nucleus/providers/storage-azure): fetched at the version released with this CLI and imported in main.go
  ldap             authentication backend (github.com/jcsvwinston/nucleus/providers/ldap): fetched at the version released with this CLI and imported in main.go
  aws-sm           secrets resolver (github.com/jcsvwinston/nucleus/providers/secrets-aws): fetched at the version released with this CLI and imported in main.go
  sentry           error reporter (github.com/jcsvwinston/nucleus/providers/errors-sentry): fetched at the version released with this CLI and imported in main.go, http_interceptors, interceptors in nucleus.yml written into the project
  stripe           billing provider (github.com/jcsvwinston/nucleus/providers/billing-stripe): fetched at the version released with this CLI and imported in main.go, .Mount(nucleus.BillingWebhook()) + billing, outbox in nucleus.yml written into the project
  oidc             federated sign-in provider, part of the framework: its import (github.com/jcsvwinston/nucleus/pkg/auth/federated/oidc) + .Mount(nucleus.FederatedSignIn()) + public_base_url, auth_federated, auth in nucleus.yml written into the project
  saml             federated sign-in provider (github.com/jcsvwinston/nucleus/providers/auth-saml): fetched at the version released with this CLI and imported in main.go, .Mount(nucleus.FederatedSignIn()) + public_base_url, auth_federated, auth in nucleus.yml written into the project
  redis-cache      cache backend, part of the framework: its import (github.com/jcsvwinston/nucleus/pkg/cache/rediscache) + cache in nucleus.yml written into the project
  apikeys          API-key authentication, part of the framework: .WithAPIKeys() written into the project
  sql-queue        job queue, part of the framework: jobs_provider in nucleus.yml written into the project
  accounts         account flows, part of the framework: .WithMail() + .Mount(accounts.FromRuntime()) + mail_driver, modules in nucleus.yml written into the project
  websockets       realtime channels, part of the framework: .WithRealtime() written into the project
  orbit            admin panel (github.com/jcsvwinston/orbit): the admin panel mounted under /admin with its own login gate, Data Studio and the live observability feed
  quark            ORM (github.com/jcsvwinston/quark): the Quark ORM (Active Record models, migrations from the model registry) for the application's domain
  quarkbridge      observability bridge (github.com/jcsvwinston/orbit/quarkbridge): a Quark middleware that publishes every statement on the observability bus, so orbit's live feed shows the SQL correlated to the request
  quarkdatasource  Data Studio adapter (github.com/jcsvwinston/orbit/quarkdatasource): the adapter that backs orbit's Data Studio with Quark models, so /admin browses and edits them

Databases (--db):
  sqlite     sqlite://app.db and drivers/sqlite (default)
  postgres   drivers/postgres (also: postgresql, pg)
  mysql      drivers/mysql
  sqlserver  drivers/mssql (also: mssql)
  oracle     drivers/oracle

Flags:
  -db string
    	Database engine the project starts on (sqlite, postgres, mysql, sqlserver, oracle): its driver module is required and imported (default "sqlite")
  -force
    	Overwrite scaffold files if the project directory exists
  -module string
    	Go module path (default: example.com/<project_name>)
  -offline
    	Do not touch the network: skip the go get of the driver and the --with entries and the go mod tidy (run them yourself before go run .)
  -out string
    	Parent directory where the project folder will be created (default ".")
  -port int
    	HTTP port in nucleus.yml (default 8080)
  -template string
    	Starter template (mvc: full-stack, api: lightweight core-only, suite: Nucleus + Quark + Orbit wired together, module: a module repository of its own) (default "mvc")
  -with string
    	Catalog entries to fetch and wire, comma-separated: the names nucleus add takes (orbit, quark, s3, ldap and the rest of nucleus add --help); --template suite implies orbit, quark, quarkbridge and quarkdatasource

Examples:
  nucleus new blog --module github.com/acme/blog
  nucleus new svc --template api --port 9090
  nucleus new shop --db postgres
  nucleus new blog --with orbit   # the admin panel mounted under /admin
  nucleus new store --template suite --db sqlite
  nucleus new greeter --template module --module github.com/acme/greeter
  nucleus new lab --offline   # no go get / go mod tidy; run them yourself

The driver module for --db and every entry --with names are resolved on the spot (go get, then go mod tidy), so the project builds as written; --offline skips all of it and hands the commands back as the next step. The driver and the modules of this repository are fetched at the versions released with this CLI; the suite products at the tag the module proxy calls latest, because their versions belong to the umbrella's certified set, which is written after this CLI is tagged.

A suite product the template does not import (quark, quarkbridge and quarkdatasource on mvc and api; only the suite template wires all four) is fetched after the tidy, which would otherwise drop it, and stays in go.mod as an indirect require until a module imports it — nucleus generate module <name> --data quark does, and the versions go.mod already carries are the ones it builds with.

Every other entry registers by its blank import, which the scaffold writes into main.go; the post-scaffold text names the configuration that selects it. An entry an import does not wire gets what nucleus add would write: the call in the nucleus.New() chain and its block in nucleus.yml.

--template module names the module after <project_name> (lowercase, words joined by underscores: the modules.<name> key and the route prefix) and its Go package after the same name without underscores. Its go.mod requires this release of the framework and the SQLite driver its test opens a database with, fetched at the version released with this CLI and tidied — or handed back by --offline.
